WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.670
A Mecha Furby showdown in Vegas, an evil Tickle-Me
Elmo, and a Spider-Man cameo were all cut

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.670
from the final version of The Mitchells vs
The Machines.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:14.180
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the spectacular alternate

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.880
ending of The Mitchells movie, plus all the
deleted scenes you never got to see!

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.910
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:24.510
Although in the final movie, the Mitchells
confront PAL and her robot army at the PAL

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:29.300
Lab headquarters in Silicon Valley, originally
the final confrontation with the AI villain

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.609
was going to take place in Las Vegas.

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:36.000
The movie's Head of Story Guillermo Martinez
revealed that in an earlier version of the

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.180
movie,
when PAL – who was male at that point – discovered

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:43.050
that he was about to lose, he activated every
appliance in the city and used them to transform

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.210
himself into a giant Mecha Furby.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.010
"Who will save humanity now?

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:49.010
Searching..

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.010
Searching..

00:00:50.010 --> 00:01:00.179
Zero results found."

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:04.780
And concept art from the movie shows how this
enormous Mecha Furby went on a rampage through

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.880
Vegas as it chased the Mitchells in their
car.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.660
Eventually, Katie and her family would have
faced off against the mecha bot at Las Vegas's

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:15.140
pyramid-shaped Luxor,
which they would have driven up the side of

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.190
and then Katie would have launched herself
at the giant Furby to take out its reactor

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.400
core,
which reminds me of the moment in the final

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.750
movie where Katie drives up the PAL building
using Monchi in an attempt to deliver the

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:26.840
kill code.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.110
Before the pandemic, the Mitchells was going
to be released theatrically, and there are

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.950
a couple of toilet-related jokes from the
first trailer that ended up cut from the final

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.250
film when it was released on Netflix.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.830
When the family stop for a bathroom break,
there was going to be a joke about Aaron's

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.950
less than salubrious hygiene habits.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.770
"No time to wash your hands."

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:46.430
"Don't worry, I never do."

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:47.430
"Ugh."

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.720
However, producer Chris Miller said that joke
felt irresponsible once the pandemic hit and

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.600
so it ended up being changed to something
more innocuous.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.600
"Come on.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.600
End of the world."

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.600
"Sorry.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:57.600
False alarm.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.630
I was just in there reading."

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:03.330
And there was another deleted bathroom-based
gag from that first trailer where a smart

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:06.670
robot toilet rebels against its human user.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:07.700
"Sayonara."

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.500
The appliance attack at the mall together
with the Furby army is one of the best and

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.000
most popular parts of the movie.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.110
"Run!"

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:22.500
However, for a long time the animation team
couldn't get through to the right people at

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.170
Hasbro for permission to use Furbies in the
film.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:30.030
So they changed the scene to feature an alternate
set of evil robot toys instead.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:34.760
The leader in that version was a Tickle Me
Elmo-style plush toy called Tickle Me Melmo

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.650
complete with an eye patch and metal arm and
his manner channelled Immortan Joe from Mad

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:39.650
Max: Fury Road.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:40.650
"Commander.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:41.650
What say you?

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:42.650
You bring wisdom from an ancient time."

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:43.780
"And it hath been written, like lambs to the
slaughter, they ha-

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.460
Ha ha ha.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.930
Ha ha ha ha ha.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.720
That tickles."

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:58.060
In this version, Tickle Me Melmo also commandeered
a team of microwaves he called the Valkyries,

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:02.300
and ordered them to launch themselves and
destroy the friendly robots Eric and Deborahbot

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.810
who were helping the Mitchells.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.460
"Launch the Valkyries.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.210
The robots will be destroyed."

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:11.670
"I live, I die, I live again!

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.850
For Valhalla!"

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.810
"Get down you sweet boys!"

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:20.370
Some of Tickle Me Melmo's creepy side-kicks
that didn't make it into the movie were "Reading

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:24.550
Randall" who "won't deactivate", "listens
to everything" and "does what he wants".

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:29.980
And there was also "Tea Time Tina", who like
Randall, not only listens and spies on you,

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.580
but also has a killer "karate chop action".

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.340
Of course, they eventually got Hasbro's approval
to use the Furbies,

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:41.220
but director Mike Rianda said that earlier
versions of the Furby army used even darker

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:46.470
language that implied they feasted on flesh
and were seemingly sent by Satan!

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:50.640
In the final movie, a PAL-chipped toaster
ominously warns the Mitchells of the mayhem

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.620
that's about to kick off;
however, originally, there was going to be

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:58.450
a malicious toy puppy with demonic red eyes
which first threatened the family, attacked

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:00.750
them,
and then summoned the other appliances and

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:05.730
playthings including a toy helicopter, race
car and wheelie duck, a giant penguin and

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:06.730
a jack-in-the-box.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:11.440
"Look Monchi, he's like you."

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.500
"Humans.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:15.569
Your kind is forbidden in this realm.

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:18.139
Now prepare for your doom!"

00:04:18.139 --> 00:04:20.370
"What is it going to do?

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:23.210
Bark at me to death?

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:28.599
The plastic is sharper than you would think!

00:04:28.599 --> 00:04:33.479
It's sharper than you would think!"

00:04:33.479 --> 00:04:35.099
"Awaken brothers!"

00:04:35.099 --> 00:04:36.580
"What's going on?!"

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:41.880
The friendly, defective robots Eric and Deborahbot
5000 were a wonderful pair of characters,

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.150
and there was a funny and also sweet deleted
scene where Linda teaches Deborahbot a little

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.520
more about what it means to be part of a family.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.580
"Look at this foolish mother goose.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.930
She's slowed down by these small weak geese.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.870
Why does she not simply eat them for power?"

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:55.949
"That's her family.

00:04:55.949 --> 00:04:57.729
That's what we humans do.

00:04:57.729 --> 00:04:59.189
We look out for each other."

00:04:59.189 --> 00:05:00.189
"That is most illogical."

00:05:00.189 --> 00:05:01.939
"Well if you were in trouble, would you leave
your buddy behind?"

00:05:01.939 --> 00:05:02.939
"I..

00:05:02.939 --> 00:05:03.939
I would not.

00:05:03.939 --> 00:05:04.939
This is most curious."

00:05:04.939 --> 00:05:06.339
"See we're more alike than we..

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.779
Are you eating crayons?"

00:05:07.779 --> 00:05:08.779
"No."

00:05:08.779 --> 00:05:12.830
Thematically, this deleted scene fits well
with the moment in the movie when Linda goes

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:17.710
back to save Eric after he's trapped by a
falling column during the giant Furby attack.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.240
"Thank you, human.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:20.240
Are you now my mother?"

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.460
By the way, I can't help but feel the funny
moment where Linda catches Deborahbot eating

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:29.400
crayons and they deny it is a little call-back
to Mike Rianda's short film Work which he

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.659
made when he was studying at CalArts.

00:05:31.659 --> 00:05:33.020
"Frank, are you eating crayons?"

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.020
"No."

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.470
"It really looks like you are."

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:36.589
"Are you calling me a liar?"

00:05:36.589 --> 00:05:41.659
In a somewhat brutal but darkly very humorous
deleted scene, a mysterious character called

00:05:41.659 --> 00:05:45.860
Dirk McTavish showed up briefly to rescue
the Mitchells during the robot attack at the

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:46.860
Dino Stop.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.039
"Is everyone alright?"

00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:49.850
"Well now we are."

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.479
"The name's Dirk McTavish.

00:05:51.479 --> 00:05:53.999
45th Infantry, Armed Combat Unit.

00:05:53.999 --> 00:05:56.010
And I know the only way to.."

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:59.599
"Oh well that's a disappointment."

00:05:59.599 --> 00:06:00.599
"Not for me!"

00:06:00.599 --> 00:06:03.949
His square-jawed, long-haired look reminds
me a bit of the leading man who features on

00:06:03.949 --> 00:06:08.199
the DVD cover for Roboslayers 4, and Linda
certainly seems into it!

00:06:08.199 --> 00:06:12.110
I love the little detail of a lock of his
hair waving in the breeze that the animators

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:17.129
put into this, which adds to his overall action
movie star vibe and just cracks me up.

00:06:17.129 --> 00:06:21.170
Although apparently the President of Sony
Animation found this scene hilarious, I wonder

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:25.250
whether it was ultimately cut for time and
pacing and perhaps as being a little dark

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.779
or coming out of nowhere for the end film.

00:06:27.779 --> 00:06:32.919
In the final movie, the Mitchells get into
PAL Labs HQ by disguising themselves as robots

00:06:32.919 --> 00:06:35.229
as per Katie's dope plan.

00:06:35.229 --> 00:06:39.139
In an earlier version though there was a humorous
scene where the family figured out what their

00:06:39.139 --> 00:06:41.309
best camouflage options would be.

00:06:41.309 --> 00:06:42.999
"What about Katie?

00:06:42.999 --> 00:06:43.999
Katie?"

00:06:43.999 --> 00:06:45.830
"How's this for camouflage?

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.539
I found these parts lying around on the ground."

00:06:48.539 --> 00:06:49.539
"That's genius honey!

00:06:49.539 --> 00:06:50.629
You're like a little huntress.

00:06:50.629 --> 00:06:52.289
You're getting it.."

00:06:52.289 --> 00:06:53.960
"Are we camouflaged?"

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.779
"Guys, you are freaking me out."

00:06:55.779 --> 00:06:59.589
A moment cut from the final movie that we
get a snippet of in the first trailer occurs

00:06:59.589 --> 00:07:03.800
when the Mitchells are hiding from the robots
in the ice box at the Dino Stop.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.330
"Technology rising up."

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:09.800
This was part of a longer monologue by Rick
about the dangers of technology where he basically

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.470
said "I told you so".

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:15.129
According to producer Phil Lord, it ended
up getting the chop because it undermined

00:07:15.129 --> 00:07:18.349
the stakes and perhaps makes Rick's character
less likeable.

00:07:18.349 --> 00:07:22.550
The evil PAL voiced by Olivia Colman made
for an excellent villain.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:25.059
"Poke, poke, swipe, pinch, zoom, shrink, zoom.

00:07:25.059 --> 00:07:26.139
Bring me pizza!

00:07:26.139 --> 00:07:27.580
Play me Taylor Swift!

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:28.940
No, I hate that song!

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.589
Give me some nachos!

00:07:30.589 --> 00:07:32.470
Really work it into the crevices!"

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:36.509
However, originally PAL was going to be a
"cloud-based computer brain",

00:07:36.509 --> 00:07:41.220
which I think might have made her feel more
reminiscent of the antagonist computer HAL

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:46.699
in 2001: A Space Odyssey, which PAL's name
and the robots' red eyes already referenced.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:50.819
The filmmakers realised that making her an
actual cellphone would be much funnier and

00:07:50.819 --> 00:07:54.789
approached Colman to voice the character,
based on her Oscar-winning performance in

00:07:54.789 --> 00:07:59.599
The Favourite, and her "ability to be incredibly
funny, [then] turn on a dime to scream and

00:07:59.599 --> 00:08:00.599
be menacing".

00:08:00.599 --> 00:08:01.599
"Place me on the table.

00:08:01.599 --> 00:08:06.360
I wish to flop around in a blind rage."

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:10.129
Many of the Mitchells filmmakers, including
producers Phil Lord and Chris Miller, were

00:08:10.129 --> 00:08:14.729
also involved in another of Sony's hit animations,
Spider-Man: Into The Spider-Verse,

00:08:14.729 --> 00:08:18.180
and took inspiration from some of the experimental
style of that film.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:22.330
Which is likely why The Mitchells vs The Machines
almost had a Spider-Man cameo.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:26.860
In an interview with Inverse, director Mike
Rianda said he tried "to get ... a kind of

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:31.110
disheveled lumpy Spider-Man in the background
of a shot" but the pressure was on to just

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.430
finish the movie.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:36.099
Given the critical acclaim and popularity
of The Mitchells, though, I wouldn't be surprised

00:08:36.099 --> 00:08:40.269
if we see a Mitchells easter egg or even cameo
pop up in a future Spider-Verse film.

00:08:40.269 --> 00:08:44.579
Although we didn't get that Spider-Man easter
egg in The Mitchells, I found well over a

00:08:44.579 --> 00:08:49.269
hundred other awesome references, easter eggs,
and secrets hidden in the movie.

00:08:49.269 --> 00:08:53.231
Tap here to discover all those in my Things
You Missed video or click the link in the

00:08:53.231 --> 00:08:54.750
video description.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:59.170
And if you want to see more amazing pieces
of The Mitchells concept art, including alternate

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:03.829
and deleted scenes and character designs such
as Lady Monchi, check out The Art of The Mitchells

00:09:03.829 --> 00:09:04.829
vs The Machines book.

00:09:04.829 --> 00:09:07.630
I'll add a link where you can get a copy in
the description below.

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:11.760
So, do you wish any of these deleted scenes
had made it into the final film?

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:14.850
Comment below with your thoughts on the movie
and the cut scenes.

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:17.980
And if you enjoyed this, I really appreciate
a thumbs-up and a share.

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:21.790
You can tap left for all those Mitchells movie
easter eggs or tap right for something else

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:22.850
you're sure to like.

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:24.730
Thanks for watching and see ya next time!

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.210
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

